# Make an orc priest and get into the dungeon.
#
# The character is a male orc priest, neutral, worshipping whichever god the
# game offers. A priest is the most demanding class to script: it has more
# choices than any other, and which choices it has depends on the god.
#
# WHY THIS SCRIPT USES CONDITIONALS AND THE OTHERS DO NOT.
#
# A key script is a fixed stream, and a fixed stream cannot answer a question
# that only sometimes gets asked. Two things vary here with the seed:
#
#   * "Choose a Domain:" appears for some gods and not others, and the list of
#     domains is the god's own. Measured 2026-08-15: seeds 852 and 893 both
#     died because of this one prompt. It had no answer in the stream, so the
#     keystroke meant for the next question answered the domain instead, and
#     everything after it was off by one.
#
#   * The size of the skill rank pool follows the god, so no fixed number of
#     RIGHT presses drains it. Character generation will not let go while a
#     rank is unspent, and a run that cannot leave the Skill Manager burns
#     every remaining key against it and reaches no map at all.
#
# Before: 98 of 100 seeds reached the dungeon. After: 100 of 100. The whole
# character now takes about 65 keystrokes rather than 200, because the loops
# stop when the work is done instead of pressing a worst-case number of times.
#
# The rank loop matches "|  *" -- the stars that count unspent ranks -- and NOT
# the "Unspent Skill Ranks" header, which stays on screen when the pool is
# empty and so never becomes false. Matching the header works but runs to the
# 200-pass limit every time.

a       # Initial Choices: [a] Create a New Character
n       # Alter the character generation options? -- no
y       # Your options will place the game in Explore Mode. Continue? -- yes
i       # Race:     [i] Orc
a       # Subrace:  [a] Orc (Standard)
g       # Class:    [g] Priest
a       # Attributes: the first of the five offered sets
c       # Alignment: [c] Neutral
a       # First feat
a       # Second feat

# Skill Manager, once for the class pool. RIGHT spends a rank on the selected
# skill and stops at that skill's maximum; DOWN moves to the next skill.
@while "Choose a Domain" a
@while "|  *" RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT DOWN
ENTER y # Done, and confirm keeping the ranks

y       # Do you wish to worship <god>? -- yes

# Again, for the pool that follows the choice of god.
@while "Choose a Domain" a
@while "|  *" RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT DOWN
ENTER y

# A priest has more to choose than a barbarian: two further feats, and a third
# pool of skill ranks that only appears once the god is known.
a a
@while "Choose a Domain" a
@while "|  *" RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT DOWN
ENTER y

a       # Personality archetype

# Four starting spells.
a a a a
